    "platform.openai.com/docs/models now 301-redirects to developers.openai.com/api/docs/models. developers.openai.com is the live canonical docs domain as of 2026-06-01.",
    "All data fetched live from official OpenAI docs; no training-knowledge fill-in. Where a detail page did not enumerate a field, it is marked null/unknown rather than invented.",
    "Reasoning-effort vocabulary has drifted across generations: GPT-5 used 'minimal'; GPT-5.1 added 'none' and dropped 'xhigh'; GPT-5.2/5.4/5.5 use the full 'none/low/medium/high/xhigh' ladder. For codex CLI dispatch the safe modern set is low/medium/high/xhigh (model_reasoning_effort), with 'none' valid on 5.2+ non-codex chat models. See per-model reasoning.effort_levels.",
    "GPT-5.5 is the current frontier flagship (GA, knowledge cutoff Dec 01 2025). GPT-5.4 is the affordable workhorse default. GPT-5.4 mini is the strongest current cost-efficient small reasoning model.",
    "GPT-5.3-Codex is the current default agentic coding model (the one to use via the codex CLI); all older Codex snapshots (5.0/5.1/5.1-Max/5.1-mini/5.2-Codex, codex-mini-latest) are now deprecated.",
    "Index/listing statuses (GA/legacy/deprecated) are taken from the /models/all listing labels; per-model detail pages add cutoffs, pricing and reasoning ladders. Several models marked 'Active/Default' on their detail page but the listing flags newer recommended replacements.",
    "Confidence: HIGH for the GPT-5.x chat/reasoning family, GPT-5.3-Codex, GPT-4.1, o3, realtime-2, image-2, embeddings (detail pages fetched). MEDIUM for models known only from the listing page (audio/tts/legacy/deprecated families) where individual detail pages were not separately fetched.",
    "gpt-5.3-chat detail page returned 404 on direct fetch; it is listed on /models/all as 'GPT-5.3 Chat - GPT-5.3 Instant model used in ChatGPT'. Use 'chat-latest' for the live ChatGPT-Instant alias (detail page confirmed).",
    "Pro variants (5.5-pro, 5.4-pro) are Responses-API-only, no streaming, no/limited cached-input discount, do NOT support structured outputs (per 5.4-pro page); use background mode to avoid timeouts."
  ],
